            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"However, this does not apply to possession of wine, beer, or distilled spirits which are:\",\n        \"(i) Manifested and transported as part of a shipment; or\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed qualification record accurately captures the statutory exception in 49 CFR 392.5(a)(3)(i), explicitly qualifying the driver possession prohibition in baseline claim C0002 when wine, beer, or distilled spirits are manifested and transported as part of a shipment. The actor, action, scope, and non-modal formulation precisely align with the regulatory source text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"quotes\": [\n        \"However, this does not apply to possession of wine, beer, or distilled spirits which are:\",\n        \"(ii) Possessed or used by bus passengers.\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed qualification record correctly captures the exception in 49 CFR 392.5(a)(3)(ii), establishing an explicit qualification edge to the possession prohibition in baseline claim C0002 for alcoholic beverages possessed or used by bus passengers. The scope, attribution, and non-modal formulation are fully faithful to the source text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
